From 5c320ca1e697288dc6fc747ed4fa1921a4faefe4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: julian_lenovo_new <julian@jc84.com>
Date: Mon, 5 Oct 2026 19:26:25 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 07/11] fix: overview gesture binds perform the bound action

Continuous overview gestures picked open vs. close from finger travel
alone: up opened and down closed, `natural-scroll=true` flipped that,
and the bound action and direction were ignored. So `open-overview` on
a swipe down, or on a swipe up with `natural-scroll=true`, could never
open the overview, and only vertical travel counted at all.

Now continuing the gesture in the direction it locked in performs the
bound action, and moving back reverses it: `open-overview` opens,
`close-overview` closes, and `toggle-overview` does whichever applies
when the gesture starts. This covers touchscreen swipes, pinches,
rotations, edge swipes (inward from the edge) and tap-hold-drags, and
touchpad swipes. `natural-scroll` no longer affects overview binds.

With `toggle-overview` bound to both swipe up and swipe down, either
direction now toggles; the docs examples use `open-overview` and
`close-overview` to keep "up opens, down closes".

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
